      <description><![CDATA[
        India&#39;s air power projection is getting a much-needed upgrade. The IAF is closing in on a ₹9,000 crore contract for six MMTT aircraft to bridge critical refueler gaps by 2030.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Deliveries are tightly scheduled between 2028 and 2030 to mitigate aging fleet issues plaguing the current Ilyushin IL-78s.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The MMTTs will vastly expand the operational radius of frontline fighters like the Su-30MKI and Rafale.
